WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.549
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:14.787
Unit seven: Personal Style. Today you will talk about self-expression with reflexive verbs.

4
00:00:15.087 --> 00:00:17.670
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:21.936
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:23.715
Aesthetic.

7
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:27.134
Aesthetic means a style or look that you like.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.761
My aesthetic is simple and clean.

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.817
Your turn. Say: Aesthetic.

10
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.621
Aesthetic.

11
00:00:37.383 --> 00:00:38.617
Self-image.

12
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:42.081
Self-image means how you see yourself.

13
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.706
Kind words help your self-image.

14
00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:47.563
Your turn. Say: Self-image.

15
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.622
Self-image.

16
00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:53.744
Confidence booster.

17
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.282
Confidence booster means something that makes you feel more confident.

18
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:01.336
A new haircut is a confidence booster.

19
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.032
Your turn. Say: Confidence booster.

20
00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.402
Confidence booster.

21
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.337
Signature look.

22
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.487
Signature look means a style that people know you for.

23
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:18.071
Her signature look is a red scarf.

24
00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:21.370
Your turn. Say: Signature look.

25
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:25.443
Signature look.

26
00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:27.556
Express yourself.

27
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.629
Express yourself means to show your feelings and ideas.

28
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:34.216
Clothes help you express yourself.

29
00:01:34.817 --> 00:01:38.050
Your turn. Say: Express yourself.

30
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.215
Express yourself.

31
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.090
Comfort zone.

32
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:49.208
Comfort zone means a situation where you feel safe and relaxed.

33
00:01:49.817 --> 00:01:52.420
Trying a new colour took me out of my comfort zone.

34
00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:55.750
Your turn. Say: Comfort zone.

35
00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.671
Comfort zone.

36
00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:01.824
Individual taste.

37
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:06.221
Individual taste means what one person personally likes.

38
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:09.281
Fashion depends on individual taste.

39
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:12.826
Your turn. Say: Individual taste.

40
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.121
Individual taste.

41
00:02:17.883 --> 00:02:18.977
Trendsetter.

42
00:02:19.983 --> 00:02:22.807
Trendsetter means a person who starts a new fashion.

43
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:25.242
She is a trendsetter at our school.

44
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.618
Your turn. Say: Trendsetter.

45
00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.421
Trendsetter.

46
00:02:33.183 --> 00:02:34.242
Versatile.

47
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.074
Versatile means useful in many different ways.

48
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:40.845
A white shirt is very versatile.

49
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:44.149
Your turn. Say: Versatile.

50
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.129
Versatile.

51
00:02:48.883 --> 00:02:49.757
Statement.

52
00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.667
Statement means something that shows a strong message.

53
00:02:54.283 --> 00:02:56.260
His bright shoes make a statement.

54
00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.584
Your turn. Say: Statement.

55
00:03:02.433 --> 00:03:03.283
Statement.

56
00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.179
Authenticity.

57
00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:09.181
Authenticity means being real and true to yourself.

58
00:03:09.783 --> 00:03:12.201
I value authenticity more than trends.

59
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:15.864
Your turn. Say: Authenticity.

60
00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.817
Authenticity.

61
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:21.712
Identity.

62
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:24.530
Identity means who you are.

63
00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:27.383
My style is part of my identity.

64
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:30.949
Your turn. Say: Identity.

65
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:34.987
Identity.

66
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.393
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.865
Visal, how would you describe your style?

68
00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.946
My aesthetic is simple: jeans, a white shirt and a cap.

69
00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.794
Is that your signature look?

70
00:03:51.883 --> 00:03:56.892
Yes! I express myself through simple, versatile clothes.

71
00:03:57.983 --> 00:03:59.495
Do you follow trends?

72
00:04:00.583 --> 00:04:06.512
Not really. I prefer authenticity. I dress myself in what I really like.

73
00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.330
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:13.773
Grammar focus: reflexive verbs (express yourself).

75
00:04:14.073 --> 00:04:15.191
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:15.883 --> 00:04:17.894
I express myself through style.

77
00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:20.783
She expresses herself through art.

78
00:04:21.683 --> 00:04:23.938
Express yourself with confidence!

79
00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:30.824
Some verbs often take a reflexive pronoun: express yourself, enjoy yourself, teach yourself.

80
00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:35.211
Be careful! Don't say: I express me through style.

81
00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:40.397
Say: I express myself through style.

82
00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:43.138
Use 'myself', not 'me', after 'express'.

83
00:04:43.933 --> 00:04:46.493
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.719
My Signature Look.

85
00:04:49.019 --> 00:04:52.702
Finding my own aesthetic helped boost my confidence and self-image.

86
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.524
I like to express myself with a signature look.

87
00:04:57.533 --> 00:05:01.669
It reflects my individual taste, not just the latest trends.

88
00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:06.315
Sometimes I step out of my comfort zone with a bold statement piece.

89
00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.286
For me, style is about authenticity and identity.

90
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.471
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:16.317 --> 00:05:18.165
She expresses blank through art.

92
00:05:18.465 --> 00:05:21.585
A, herself. B, himself. C, her.

93
00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:26.796
The answer is A: herself.

94
00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.402
A style that people know you for is a blank.

95
00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:35.795
A, signature look. B, comfort zone. C, self-image.

96
00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:41.553
The answer is A: signature look.

97
00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:44.925
Useful in many different ways is blank.

98
00:05:45.225 --> 00:05:49.784
A, versatile. B, authentic. C, aesthetic.

99
00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:55.623
The answer is A: versatile.

100
00:05:56.833 --> 00:05:59.706
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:03.269
How does your personal style reflect who you are?

102
00:06:12.083 --> 00:06:13.700
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:24.875
My style is calm and simple, like my personality. I express myself through colours. Blue is my favourite, and it makes me feel confident.

104
00:06:25.175 --> 00:06:27.035
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:32.971
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and reflexive verbs (express yourself).

106
00:06:33.271 --> 00:06:36.817
Today's value is self-confidence. Believe in yourself.

107
00:06:37.117 --> 00:06:39.363
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

108
00:06:39.663 --> 00:06:43.918
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

